# Environment file for Security News Aggregator

# Optional: Proxy used by crawlers (helps when target sites block requests from your network)
# The code prefers HTTPS_PROXY and falls back to HTTP_PROXY; either may be set.
# Leave both commented out to use a direct connection.
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:10808
# HTTP_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:10808

# AI Curation (supports OpenAI-compatible APIs)
# Requires AI_API_KEY to be configured
# AI_API_KEY=sk-your_api_key_here
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Fetch proxy for datacenter-blocked sources (optional, shared worker)
# When set, scrapers for sources that block datacenter IPs route through
# this Cloudflare Worker: X fetches worker-first (x.com blocks both
# datacenter and most residential IPs) and FreeBuf direct-first with the
# worker as fallback (freebuf.com blocks only datacenter IPs like the CI
# runner's; Cloudflare egress works for both). Falls back to a direct
# connection when unset or on any fetch failure.
# X_PROXY_BASE must include the https:// scheme — a bare domain is an
# invalid URL and the proxy path silently falls back to direct.
# See x-proxy-worker/README.md for deployment.
# X_PROXY_BASE=https://secnews-x-proxy.your-subdomain.workers.dev
# X_PROXY_TOKEN=your_worker_token
